they came to the center of rio de  janeiro by  foot and even on piggyback to protest  against president jair bolsonaro  in his response to the covet 19 pandemic  the protesters blamed the president for  downplaying the virus  with thousands still dying every day and  for taking too long to start the  inoculation campaign  there were posters comparing bolsonaro  to adolf hitler  and accusing him of genocide carina  munoz  says the opposition has been avoiding  the streets  in a country with the world's second  largest covid19 death toll  that can do so no longer  we should all be at home keeping  ourselves safe but we've reached a point  where we can no longer remain silent  we have to show the world that we are  against bolsonaro's denialism  if we continue to keep quiet while he's  holding rallies all over brazil  it'll seem like brazilians are complicit  with his attitudes and we are  not last week bolsonaro led a motorbike  rally in rio de janeiro  gathering crowds and scorning the mask  he's on the campaign trail  and planning more of the same  his opponents say they felt compelled to  respond  but the organizers of saturday's  nationwide protest  insisted people wear their masks while  making their demands  although it wasn't just about the  pandemic  one man came out against bolsonaro and  in favor of a free palestine  people here are asking for many things  for better public education  for better public health for vaccines  they're also asking for illegal mining  to stop an indigenous  lands but what they all want in common  is president bolsonaro's  there were protests also in the capital  brasilia  and in hundreds of other brazilian  cities the impeachment they're demanding  seems unlikely for now but the  opposition is trying for a united front  against bolsonaro  to be ready for next year's presidential  elections  monika yanakev al-jazeera rio de janeiro
 

